---
// Image With Text section (Task 4, Course PDP Chunk B2; review fix wave —
// Chunk B2 follow-up — below) — Figma file FX7PDNvhZwyozODaq8Q8i7. Prop is
// `{ item }` (same shape as every other PDP section), reading
// `item.pdp.imageWithText`. This is the 15th and FINAL registry type for the
// PDP composer (see Pdp.astro's own header comment for the running count) —
// a plain media/text split: an image beside a heading + bullet list, with
// FIVE OPTIONAL pieces (an intro line, a list "lead-in" sentence, a
// post-list note paragraph, a data-driven media-column width, and a trailing
// CTA button with an optional trailing icon).
//
// ---- BUILT AGAINST ALL FOUR KNOWN INSTANCES, NOT JUST THE FIRST ONE --------
// This section has FOUR instances in Figma TODAY, not one. A first review
// pass (Task 4 itself) skimmed only ONE of Foot Fest's three instances
// (674:7750) plus a metadata-only glance at the other two, and wrongly
// generalized "Foot Fest is image-RIGHT" from that single sample — WRONG:
// two of Foot Fest's own three instances are image-LEFT. A second review
// re-pulled all four instances individually; this is that corrected,
// per-instance record (desktop nodes; ✓ = present, – = absent):
//
//   | Node      | Course            | Image | Media col          | intro | listLead | items | note | CTA            | icon |
//   |-----------|-------------------|-------|---------------------|-------|----------|-------|------|----------------|------|
//   | 686:6540  | Trainer Cert      | LEFT  | w-374 / min-h-250   | –     | –        | 7     | –    | –              | –    |
//   | 674:7748  | Foot Fest onsite  | LEFT  | w-374 / min-h-250   | –     | –        | 3     | –    | "Grab your room"| no  |
//   | 674:7750  | Foot Fest VIP     | RIGHT | flex-1 / min-h-500  | ✓     | ✓        | 6     | –    | "Become A VIP" | YES  |
//   | 674:7752  | Foot Fest walk    | LEFT  | flex-1 / min-h-500  | –     | ✓        | 3     | YES  | "Register Now" | YES  |
//
// (Mobile: Trainer Cert's own mobile frame is 1116:17403; Foot Fest's is
// 1098:13857 for the VIP instance — see the mobile-stacking note below.)
//
// Only Trainer Certification's data ships in this task/branch — the other
// three rows exist purely to shape this component's contract so a later
// chunk (Foot Fest) can ship as pure data, no component edit. Two real
// per-field takeaways from re-pulling all four, not assumed:
//
//   - The media column is NOT one fixed size. 686:6540/674:7748 both measure
//     a literal 374px-wide, 250px-min-height column; 674:7750/674:7752 are
//     instead an even ~50/50 `flex-[1_0_0]`/`min-h-[500px]` split — a
//     genuinely different shape, not a rounding difference. Hardcoding
//     374/250 (Task 4's original code) would have shipped a ~30%-wide,
//     half-height, `object-fit:cover`-cropped image column on two of the
//     four instances. See `imageWidth` below.
//   - 674:7752 has REAL copy after its `<ul>` ("* Can't join us in person?
//     You can still donate and join the walk virtually!") that neither
//     `intro` nor `listLead` can express (both render ABOVE the list). See
//     `note` below.
//
// This precedent already produced THIRTEEN separate "component hardcoded to
// whichever page happened to be built first" defects on this branch (see
// ThreeColumnInfo.astro's own header comment for the fullest account) — so
// every field below, and the CSS approach for `imageSide`/`imageWidth`, is
// shaped by ALL FOUR instances even though only Trainer Certification's data
// ships today.
//
// ---- Data shape --------------------------------------------------------
// `item.pdp.imageWithText` = `{ image, imageSide?, imageWidth?, heading,
// intro?, listLead?, items: [string], note?, cta?: { label, href, icon? } }`.
// `imageSide` is `'left'` (default) | `'right'`. `imageWidth` is a literal
// px number (`374` for 686:6540/674:7748's shape); ABSENT means the ~50/50
// `flex-[1_0_0]`/500px-min-height split (674:7750/674:7752's shape) — see
// the CSS section below for why this is the default, not the opt-in. `cta`
// is `{ label, href, icon? }` — `icon` is an optional boolean (674:7750/
// 674:7752's CTAs both have a trailing arrow; 674:7748's does not, so this
// is genuinely per-instance, not a fixed CTA style).
//
// Trainer Certification's own entry sets `image`/`heading`/`items` ONLY —
// every other field is OMITTED entirely in catalog.js (its own Figma frame
// has none of them), which is what proves they're genuinely optional rather
// than merely unused — see catalog.js's own comment on this item's
// `imageWithText` block, and this task's report for the `dist/` grep that
// confirms no empty `<p>`/note/CTA/non-default media column ships.
//
// ---- Guards check NON-EMPTINESS, not presence (10+ prior instances) ------
// `items` is the one required field; every other STRING/OBJECT field is a
// bare `&&` guard on a plain (possibly absent) value — `''`/`undefined` are
// both falsy in JS, so no extra `.length` check is needed for `intro`/
// `listLead`/`note`/`heading` the way ThreeColumnInfo.astro's `columns`/`cta`
// (arrays/objects, where `[]`/`{}` are truthy) require one. `cta` IS guarded
// on `label && href` both present (not just the object's presence), matching
// ThreeColumnInfo.astro's own `hasCta` idiom — a `cta: {}` or `cta: {
// label }` value must not render an empty/href-less button; `cta.icon` is
// additionally gated on `hasCta` itself (an icon with no button to sit in
// makes no sense). Absent/empty -> renders NOTHING: no empty `<p>`, no empty
// lead-in/note, no empty button, no icon on a CTA-less section — the exact
// bug class this file exists to not repeat.
//
// ---- `imageSide` — CSS-only flip, not a duplicated markup branch --------
// The component ALWAYS renders markup in one fixed order — media, then
// body (heading/intro/lead/list/cta) — matching Trainer Certification's own
// DOM order on both its frames. `imageSide: 'right'` (Foot Fest's future
// case) flips the VISUAL order at desktop only, via `flex-direction:
// row-reverse` keyed off a `data-image-side` attribute — never a second,
// parallel "image after text" markup branch, per this task's explicit
// brief. This keeps a single source of truth for the list/CTA markup
// regardless of which side the image renders on.
//
// Mobile does NOT follow `imageSide` at all: Foot Fest's own VIP mobile pull
// (1098:13857, one of its 3 mobile Image With Text instances) shows the
// image FIRST (above the text), the IDENTICAL stacking order Trainer
// Certification's own mobile frame (1116:17403) uses — even though that same
// VIP instance's DESKTOP frame (674:7750) is image-RIGHT. I.e. mobile always
// stacks image-above-text regardless of the desktop side, confirmed by
// pulling BOTH mobile instances rather than assumed from `imageSide` —
// exactly the check this task's brief warned not to skip. So the
// `row-reverse` override below is scoped inside the `@media (min-width:
// 1024px)` block only; the mobile base layout is a plain column with no
// reordering.
//
// ---- Image `alt` ---------------------------------------------------------
// Both known instances' images are decorative lifestyle/lifestyle-adjacent
// shots (a hands-on workshop demo for Trainer Cert, a flat VIP-ticket
// graphic for Foot Fest) sitting beside a heading that already carries the
// section's full meaning — same reasoning InstructorCard.astro's own
// placeholder-photo precedent already established (`alt=""`, cited there
// for the identical reason: a generic/stand-in image with no informational
// content of its own beyond what the adjacent text already states). `alt=""`
// is used here for the same reason, not because these images are
// unimportant, but because a screen-reader user loses nothing skipping past
// them when the heading + list already say everything the section
// communicates.
//
// ---- CTA -------------------------------------------------------------
// `isExternalHref` (`src/scripts/links.js`) is this repo's one shared
// internal/external link predicate (already used by ComparisonChart.astro's
// CTA, CourseDetails.astro's enroll CTA, and ThreeColumnInfo.astro's own
// CTA) — reused here rather than a fourth copy of the same `/^https?:/`
// regex. Trainer Certification sets no `cta` at all, so this is inert for
// this task's own shipped page; Foot Fest's future "Become A VIP"/"Register
// Now" buttons (an on-page anchor/route, not yet confirmed internal or
// external) are the first real exerciser of this branch.
//
// `cta.icon` (review fix wave) — a trailing arrow, gated on `hasCta &&
// Boolean(cta.icon)`. 674:7750 (VIP) and 674:7752 (Fundraiser Walk) both
// show a 24px white arrow with a 12px (`--space-3`) gap from the label;
// 674:7748 (Stay Onsite) shows the SAME filled teal button with NO icon — a
// genuinely per-instance difference, not a fixed CTA style, hence a field on
// `cta` rather than something the component always renders whenever `cta`
// is set. The icon is NOT `/images/nav/arrow.svg` (checked, not reused): that
// asset is a solid filled chevron-arrow shape built for a different UI (nav
// mega-menu cards / PLP CTA rows — see `NavCard.astro`/`CrossSell.astro`);
// Figma's own button icon is a thin open-stroke line arrow, the exact
// mismatch Testimonial.astro's own header comment already documents for its
// carousel arrows ("neither existing repo icon in `/images/nav/` matches its
// thin open-stroke chevron shape ... a small inline stroke-arrow SVG is
// built here instead of reusing either"). This file reuses that exact same
// precedent: `ARROW_PATH` below is Testimonial.astro's own path constant
// (`M4 12H20M20 12L14 6M20 12L14 18`), rendered inline with
// `stroke="currentColor"` so it inherits the CTA's own white text colour
// automatically (no separate colour token/prop needed) — not a third copy
// of the same inline SVG.
//
// ---- Tokens / literals -----------------------------------------------
// Heading = --type-h3 (600/32px) — Figma's own desktop pull binds it to
// `var(--text-h3,32px)`; mobile's pull shows the SAME token with a 24px
// fallback instead. This repo's tokens.css has one non-responsive --type-h3
// (32px), and every sibling course section (CourseDetails, CourseOverview,
// FourColumn, ThreeColumnInfo's own column sub-heading) already keeps a
// single type token consistent across both breakpoints rather than
// introducing a one-off mobile override — same choice here.
//
// List item text is a genuine breakpoint-specific case, not a token
// mismatch to paper over: desktop's own pull binds the list to
// `var(--text-body-sm,14px)`; mobile's own pull (BOTH Trainer Cert's
// 1116:17403 and Foot Fest's 1098:13857) instead binds it to
// `var(--text-body,16px)`. This repo's tokens.css already carries a
// dedicated `--type-body-16` (400/16px/1.4) token for exactly this
// fallback value (used by Testimonial.astro/YoullStopAndInstead.astro/
// CartDrawer.astro/PlpCard.astro/PromoCard.astro/QuickAddModal.astro for
// the identical Figma `--text-body,16px` binding — see those files' own
// header comments), distinct from `--type-body` (20px), which does NOT
// match Figma's 16px fallback here. So: `--type-body-sm` at desktop,
// `--type-body-16` at the mobile-first base — a real, Figma-confirmed
// responsive font-size difference, not an invented one.
//
// List item spacing is also breakpoint-specific and literal-free: desktop's
// own pull shows `mb-[8px]` per `<li>` (an exact `--space-2` match); mobile's
// shows `mb-[24px]` (an exact `--space-5` match) — both real DS-token hits,
// no literals needed for the vertical rhythm. Bullet indent (`ms-*`) is the
// one literal pair: mobile's `ms-[24px]` is again an exact `--space-5`
// match, but desktop's own `ms-[21px]` lands nowhere on this repo's --space
// scale (16/24 bracket it) — same "literal OK, flagged" allowance
// ThreeColumnInfo.astro's own 20px list-item gap already takes.
//
// Section-level rhythm: desktop's own outer wrapper shows `gap-64
// px-48 py-64` — all three land exactly on this repo's scale (--space-8,
// --space-7, --space-8), so no literals there either. Mobile's image is a
// plain `aspect-[430/410]` box, reproduced as a literal aspect-ratio.
//
// ---- `imageWidth` — data-driven media column, not a hardcoded 374px -----
// (Review fix wave.) Task 4's original CSS hardcoded the desktop media
// column to `flex: 0 0 374px; width: 374px; min-height: 250px` — 686:6540
// (Trainer Cert) and 674:7748 (Stay Onsite)'s own shape, measured off the
// 1200-wide desktop frame (same "literal measured column width" idiom
// CourseDetails' 484px buybox/ThreeColumnInfo's 761px heading already use),
// but NOT 674:7750 (VIP)/674:7752 (Fundraiser Walk)'s — both of those
// instead measure `flex-[1_0_0]`/`min-h-[500px]`, an even ~50/50 split. Two
// of the four known instances would have shipped a ~30%-wide, half-height,
// `object-fit:cover`-cropped image column under the old hardcode.
//
// `imageWidth` (optional px number) now drives this: ABSENT is the DEFAULT
// (`flex: 1 1 0; min-height: 500px` — the ~50/50 split), not the opt-in,
// because the ~50/50 shape is what an as-yet-unauthored instance is more
// likely to need if a future course's own Image With Text frame doesn't
// happen to match Trainer Cert's specific 374/250 measurement — Trainer
// Certification sets `imageWidth: 374` explicitly. `min-height: 250px` is
// NOT a separate field: it's a fixed pairing with the fixed-width branch
// (both Figma instances that use a fixed width use exactly this
// min-height), same "component-intrinsic literal, not requiring its own
// data hook" treatment `.image-with-text__cta`'s 20px padding already takes.
// Implemented via a `--image-with-text-media-width` CSS custom property (set
// as an inline `style` on the section only when `imageWidth` is present) and
// a `[data-media-fixed='true']` attribute selector — not a duplicated markup
// branch, matching this file's own `imageSide` CSS-only-flip precedent.
//
// Mobile's OUTER wrapper carries no horizontal padding at all (the image
// bleeds full-width edge to edge, `py-64` only) while its BODY block alone
// carries `px-24` (an exact `--space-5` match) — the same "full-bleed media,
// inset text" idiom FourColumn.astro's own mobile card already documents.
//
// ---- Desktop/mobile CONTENT divergence (disclosed here + this task's own
// report; canonical value per this task's "pull desktop first" rule) -------
// Trainer Certification's own heading DISAGREES between breakpoints, not
// just in size: desktop (686:6540) reads "Additional Benefits of the Gait
// Happens Trainer Certification"; mobile (1116:17403) reads "Additional
// Benefits of the GH Trainer Certification" (the brand name abbreviated to
// initials). The 7 bullet items agree byte-for-byte on both frames — only
// the heading shortens. Desktop's full-name wording is kept canonical below
// (same "pull desktop first, flag mobile's divergence" precedent every
// other course section on this branch already follows), per this task's own
// report.
//
// ---- `note` — a post-list paragraph, not a duplicated intro/lead --------
// (Review fix wave.) 674:7752 (Fundraiser Walk) renders one more paragraph
// AFTER its `<ul>`: "* Can't join us in person? You can still donate and
// join the walk virtually!" — neither `intro` nor `listLead` can express
// this (both render ABOVE the list, matching Trainer Certification's own
// DOM order, which has no post-list content at all). `note` is a plain
// OPTIONAL string, bare `&&`-guarded, rendered immediately after the `<ul>`;
// absent (every instance except 674:7752's future data) renders nothing.
// Same typography as `intro`/`listLead` (Figma's own text block runs all of
// intro/lead/list/note through one font binding), so it's added to that
// existing selector group rather than a new type rule.
import { isExternalHref } from '../../scripts/links.js';

// Testimonial.astro's own arrow-icon path (see that file's header comment
// for why: neither `/images/nav/arrow.svg` nor `arrow-lg.svg` match Figma's
// thin open-stroke arrow glyph, both being solid filled shapes for a
// different UI). Reused verbatim here for the CTA's optional trailing icon
// rather than a third copy of the same inline SVG — see this file's own
// "CTA" section above.
const ARROW_PATH = 'M4 12H20M20 12L14 6M20 12L14 18';

const { item } = Astro.props;
const data = item.pdp?.imageWithText;
const items = data?.items ?? [];
const imageSide = data?.imageSide === 'right' ? 'right' : 'left';
const imageWidth = data?.imageWidth;
const cta = data?.cta;
const hasCta = Boolean(cta?.label && cta?.href);
const hasCtaIcon = hasCta && Boolean(cta.icon);
const isExternal = hasCta ? isExternalHref(cta.href) : false;
---
{items.length > 0 && (
  <section
    class="image-with-text"
    data-pdp-id={item.id}
    data-image-side={imageSide}
    data-media-fixed={imageWidth ? 'true' : undefined}
    style={imageWidth ? `--image-with-text-media-width: ${imageWidth}px` : undefined}
  >
    <div class="image-with-text__inner">
      <div class="image-with-text__media">
        <img src={data.image} alt="" loading="lazy" />
      </div>
      <div class="image-with-text__body">
        {data.heading && <h2 class="image-with-text__heading">{data.heading}</h2>}
        {data.intro && <p class="image-with-text__intro">{data.intro}</p>}
        {data.listLead && <p class="image-with-text__lead">{data.listLead}</p>}
        <ul class="image-with-text__list">
          {items.map((text) => <li>{text}</li>)}
        </ul>
        {data.note && <p class="image-with-text__note">{data.note}</p>}
        {hasCta && (
          <a
            class="image-with-text__cta"
            href={cta.href}
            {...(isExternal ? { target: '_blank', rel: 'noopener noreferrer' } : {})}
          >
            {cta.label}
            {hasCtaIcon && (
              <svg
                class="image-with-text__cta-icon"
                width="24"
                height="24"
                viewBox="0 0 24 24"
                fill="none"
                aria-hidden="true"
              >
                <path d={ARROW_PATH} stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" />
              </svg>
            )}
          </a>
        )}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
)}
<style>
  .image-with-text__inner {
    max-width: var(--container-max);
    margin-inline: auto;
    padding-block: var(--space-8);
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-8);
  }

  .image-with-text__media {
    width: 100%;
    aspect-ratio: 430 / 410;
    overflow: hidden;
    background: var(--color-border);
    flex-shrink: 0;
  }
  .image-with-text__media img {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    object-fit: cover;
  }

  .image-with-text__body {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: flex-start;
    gap: var(--space-6);
    padding-inline: var(--space-5);
    width: 100%;
    min-width: 0;
  }

  .image-with-text__heading {
    font: var(--type-h3);
    color: var(--color-ink);
  }

  .image-with-text__intro,
  .image-with-text__lead,
  .image-with-text__note {
    font: var(--type-body-16);
    color: var(--color-ink);
  }

  .image-with-text__list {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    width: 100%;
    /* --space-5 (24px) — exact match to mobile's own `ms-[24px]` bullet
       indent (see header comment). */
    padding-inline-start: var(--space-5);
    margin: 0;
  }
  .image-with-text__list li {
    font: var(--type-body-16);
    color: var(--color-ink);
    /* --space-5 (24px) — exact match to mobile's own `mb-[24px]` per-item
       gap (see header comment). */
    margin-bottom: var(--space-5);
  }
  .image-with-text__list li:last-child {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .image-with-text__cta {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    /* --space-3 (12px) — exact match to Figma's own `gap-[var(--space-12,
       12px)]` between the CTA label and its optional trailing icon (see
       header comment). No-op whenever `cta.icon` is unset (a single-child
       flex row ignores `gap`). */
    gap: var(--space-3);
    background: var(--color-teal);
    color: var(--color-paper);
    font: var(--type-button);
    /* 20px literal — same figure CourseDetails' enroll CTA /
       ComparisonChart's CTA / ThreeColumnInfo's CTA already flag; this
       repo's --space scale has 16/24 on either side of it, no exact step. */
    padding: var(--space-4) 20px;
    text-decoration: none;
    text-align: center;
    transition: transform var(--motion-fast) var(--ease-standard);
  }
  .image-with-text__cta:hover {
    transform: translateY(-2px);
  }
  /* Optional trailing icon (674:7750/674:7752 — see header comment).
     `stroke="currentColor"` on the inline `<path>` already inherits
     `.image-with-text__cta`'s own `color: var(--color-paper)`; this rule
     only needs to stop the icon from flex-shrinking against a long label. */
  .image-with-text__cta-icon {
    flex-shrink: 0;
  }
  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
    .image-with-text__cta:hover {
      transform: none;
    }
  }

  /* ---- Desktop (Figma 686:6540, ≥1024) --------------------------------- */
  @media (min-width: 1024px) {
    .image-with-text__inner {
      flex-direction: row;
      align-items: stretch;
      padding-inline: var(--space-7);
    }
    /* Default media column shape: the ~50/50 split 674:7750 (VIP)/674:7752
       (Fundraiser Walk) both use — see header comment on why this, not a
       fixed width, is the default. Overridden below when `imageWidth` is
       set (686:6540/674:7748's shape). */
    .image-with-text__media {
      flex: 1 1 0;
      aspect-ratio: auto;
      min-height: 500px;
    }
    /* `imageWidth` (review fix wave) — Trainer Cert's own 374px/250px shape.
       `--image-with-text-media-width` is set as an inline style on the
       `<section>` only when `item.pdp.imageWithText.imageWidth` is present
       (see the frontmatter/markup above); `min-height: 250px` is a fixed
       pairing with this branch, not itself data-driven (see header
       comment). Absent (674:7750/674:7752's future data) never matches this
       selector, leaving the default ~50/50 split above untouched. */
    .image-with-text[data-media-fixed='true'] .image-with-text__media {
      flex: 0 0 var(--image-with-text-media-width);
      width: var(--image-with-text-media-width);
      min-height: 250px;
    }
    .image-with-text__body {
      flex: 1 1 0;
      min-width: 0;
      padding-inline: 0;
    }
    /* `imageSide: 'right'` (Foot Fest's future case) — a CSS-only flip, not
       a duplicated markup branch. Desktop only; mobile always stacks
       image-above-text regardless of this attribute (see header comment). */
    .image-with-text[data-image-side='right'] .image-with-text__inner {
      flex-direction: row-reverse;
    }
    .image-with-text__intro,
    .image-with-text__lead,
    .image-with-text__note {
      font: var(--type-body-sm);
    }
    .image-with-text__list li {
      font: var(--type-body-sm);
      /* 21px literal — desktop's own `ms-[21px]` bullet indent lands
         nowhere on this repo's --space scale (16/24 bracket it); see
         header comment. */
      margin-bottom: var(--space-2);
    }
    .image-with-text__list {
      padding-inline-start: 21px;
    }
  }
</style>
